<title>USA: Imax, Showscan settle litigation.</title>
<headline>Imax, Showscan settle litigation.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imax Corp and Showscan Entertainment Inc said Friday that they had entered into a global pact to settle litigation between them.</p>
<p>Terms of the settlement were not disclosed, and the settlement agreement is not expected to have a material financial effect on either party, a joint statement from the companies said.</p>
<p>According to Imax's annual report, Showscan had sued Imax over antitrust issues, and Imax had sued Showscan for trademark infringment.</p>
<p>U.S.-based Showscan is one of the world's largest providers of simulated rides and has been seeking to enter the giant screen cinema market in Australia with a local partner, Reality Cinemas.</p>
<p>((Carol Huang -- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
